 4. 🦖 1 science thing: Big dino find 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Left: The excavation crew with the tracks. Right: An isolated track. Photos courtesy Tyler Lyson Scientists have retraced the steps of a Tyrannosaurus rex that went for a stroll 66 million years ago across what's now North Dakota, Axios Denver's Alayna Alvarez reports. 

 They say the finding is the first known trackway left by an adult T. rex. 🪏 Paleontologists from the Denver Museum of Nature &amp; Science and Liverpool John Moores University, who jointly made the discovery, say the find offers a rare look at how the iconic dinosaur moved.

 Their discovery was published this week in the "Journal of Vertebrate Paleontology." Go deeper . 

 
 
